 ],
 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 4.25,
   "text": "There's an old idea in psychology called the *Zeigarnik* effect."
  },
  {
   "start": 4.3,
   "end": 11.05,
   "text": "It's named after Bluma *Zeigarnik*, a psychologist who suggested that the mind doesn't like *unfinished* tasks."
  },
  {
   "start": 11.1,
   "end": 15.35,
   "text": "People tend to remember *unfinished* things *better* than finished ones."
  },
  {
   "start": 15.4,
   "end": 21.65,
   "text": "Think of a browser with too many *tabs* *open*. Each *unfinished* thing is a *tab*."
  },
  {
   "start": 21.7,
   "end": 29.55,
   "text": "You don't see them while you're busy. But when you sit still, the quiet makes them easy to hear."
  },
  {
   "start": 29.6,
   "end": 36.35,
   "text": "A *2011* study by Masicampo and Baumeister tested this. They gave people goals they hadn't finished."
  },
  {
   "start": 36.4,
   "end": 42.25,
   "text": "Those goals kept popping up in their minds, even during an unrelated reading task."
  },
  {
   "start": 42.3,
   "end": 46.25,
   "text": "People's performance on a word puzzle got worse too."
  },
  {
   "start": 46.3,
   "end": 51.35,
   "text": "So the *mug* isn't really about the *mug*. It's an *open* *tab*."
  },
  {
   "start": 51.4,
   "end": 55.35,
   "text": "There's a second layer. Guilt about leisure is common."
  },
  {
   "start": 55.4,
   "end": 62.15,
   "text": "In a survey of 530 adults, people who watched less TV overall felt guiltier about binge-watching."
  },
  {
   "start": 62.2,
   "end": 70.05,
   "text": "A recent European interview study found that people often feel their free time isn't meaningful enough, and *guilt* follows."
  },
  {
   "start": 70.1,
